#: ../../start-here.rst:-1
#: 1da11606c1e64021b68c27bc050bdc02
msgid "The best way to get started with Diátaxis is by applying it to documentation problems."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:7
#: d1a5c859d6e64c9598c4b8e8e7cb5de2
msgid "Start here - Diátaxis in five minutes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:11
#: 82849d38fe9b42afb3a2b309433bce79
msgid "Treat this website as a handbook or a toolbox that you make use of when you need it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:13
#: e6f385a23f994b68bf5bdaeeb684d36e
msgid "You don't need to read everything on this website to make sense of Diátaxis, or to start using it in practice. In fact I recommend that you don't. **The best way to get started with Diátaxis is by applying it** - to something, however small."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:15
#: cf31b1c5c26b434490f9904f512c6feb
msgid "Read this page for a brief primer. Each section contains links to more in-depth material; refer to that when you need it - when you're actually at work, or reflecting on the documentation problems you have encountered."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:20
#: 76acb671b53545d0b55ba568d8a6c5e4
msgid "The four kinds of documentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:22
#: 476509a37507458296cd9ad735e8711c
msgid "The core idea of Diátaxis is that there are fundamentally four identifiable kinds of documentation, that respond to four different needs. The four kinds are: *tutorials*, *how-to guides*, *reference* and *explanation*. Each has a different purpose, and needs to be written in a different way."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:26
#: c1961caf0bf34adc9cddd0182bab6ff4
msgid "Tutorials"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:30
#: e7770b00aeb1493b9a426d6f653cbd5f
msgid ":ref:`Tutorials in more detail <tutorials>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:31
#: b5a3f0a7c48c4228b8ec9bd499ab8e23
msgid ":ref:`Why tutorials are completely different from how-to guides <tutorials-how-to>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:33
#: 83203167cca34db8955bd90db5db8b20
msgid "**A tutorial is a lesson**, that takes a student by the hand through a learning experience. A tutorial is always *practical*: the user *does* something, under the guidance of an instructor. A tutorial is designed around an encounter that the learner can make sense of, in which the instructor is responsible for the learner's safety and success."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:35
#: 478ef9bb3af6475e808ddc98be6aa4bf
msgid "A driving lesson is a good example of a tutorial. The purpose of the lesson is to develop skills and confidence in the student, not to get from A to B. A software example could be: *Let's create a simple game in Python*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:37
#: bbbb61e421de4410ac0e02e80abc593c
msgid "*The user will learn through what they do* - not because someone has tried to teach them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:39
#: c0af145dd56e4ad88506489dfdc48cf4
msgid "In documentation, the special difficulty is that the instructor is condemned to be absent, and is not there to monitor the learner and correct their mistakes. The instructor must somehow find a way to be present through written instruction alone."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:43
#: 2a793e7adf5246ceb2ace138e5862cc8
msgid "How-to guides"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:47
#: f3830b9360c5414899a1ad9e907986d4
msgid ":ref:`How-to guides in more detail <how-to>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:49
#: e3fd57a6649240159c849bdf06cbd90c
msgid "**A how-to guide addresses a real-world goal or problem**, by providing practical directions to help the user who is in that situation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:51
#: 869a18f166f640afb2962d716249ece1
msgid "A how-to guide always addresses an already-competent user, who is expected to be able to use the guide to help them get their work done. In contrast to a tutorial, a how-to guide is concerned with *work* rather than *study*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:53
#: e5d4c44732c14cbf9296797722dd0edf
msgid "A how-to guide might be: *How to store cellulose nitrate film* (in motion picture photography) or *How to configure frame profiling* (in software). Or even: *Troubleshooting deployment problems*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:57
#: a7a7011cdbe04cf7bb91052f17307e33
msgid "Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:61
#: ad2d135a002e470aad3eede3db172ef3
msgid ":ref:`Reference in more detail <reference>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:63
#: c3b2984e90f848c4bca9b4ee1a136f9a
msgid "**Reference guides contain the technical description** - facts - that a user needs in order to do things correctly: accurate, complete, reliable information, free of distraction and interpretation. They contain *propositional or theoretical knowledge*, not guides to action."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:65
#: e954f94736fa4244b9de38de0b07370d
msgid "Like a how-to guide, reference documentation serves the user who is at *work*, and it's up to the user to be sufficiently competent to interpret and use it correctly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:67
#: f1aa2461b0da47878497677cfdd72cd2
msgid "*Reference material is neutral.* It is not concerned with what the user is doing. A marine chart could be used by a ship's navigator to plot a course, but equally well by a prosecuting magistrate in a legal case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:69
#: 9aff82b2ce154465a6861950bffb40a0
msgid "Where possible, the architecture of reference documentation should reflect the structure or architecture of the thing it's describing - just like a map does. If a method is part of a class that belongs to a certain module, then we should expect to see the same relationship in the documentation too."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:73
#: 9edb9de666fe4065856d8e2dbebee14f
msgid "Explanation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:77
#: 7f09e0a585a94f4f81e9d3dc2556fdd5
msgid ":ref:`Explanation in more detail <explanation>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:78
#: c60e3f6571704eb88b18420f5e36a6fe
msgid ":ref:`Understanding the difference between reference and explanation <reference-explanation>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:81
#: 03316c5bae854fdc9f1638e9282bb22a
msgid "**Explanatory guides provide context and background.** They serve the need to understand and put things in a bigger picture. Explanation joins things together, and helps answer the question *why?*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:83
#: 23fe8b38d321450d878d1d18b3ed1efe
msgid "Explanation often needs to circle around its subject, and approach it from different directions. It can contain opinions and take perspectives."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:85
#: ce7fb9724519482b8988fbb2f082936f
msgid "Like reference, explanation belongs to the realm of propositional knowledge rather than action. However its purpose is to serve the user's study - as tutorials do - and not their work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:87
#: f953cf22b9224a228ead4ff6db6f2486
msgid "Often, writers of tutorials who are anxious that their students should *know* things overload their tutorials with distracting and unhelpful explanation. It would be much more useful to give the learner the most minimal explanation (\"Here, we use HTTPS because it's safer\") and then link to an in-depth article (*Secure communication using HTTPS encryption*) for when the user is ready for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:93
#: ca15176a6c7e4de89c3cc0e0fa2efd3d
msgid "The Diátaxis map"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:95
#: ad20647a0fa04209b0c1fcbeee434f1b
msgid "The four kinds of documentation and the relationships between them can be summarised in the Diátaxis map."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:99
#: d3de42b3dda7472b89d62b2f8a95b759
msgid ":ref:`The map in more detail <map>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:101
#: 37f303b7fc8340b8b388b09dbb689de1
msgid "Diátaxis is not just a list of four different things, but a conceptual arrangement of them. It shows how the four kinds of documentation are related to each other, and distinct from each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:103
#: 63095868d9594132b03c2e9dad895478
msgid "Crossing or blurring the boundaries described in the map is at the heart of a vast number of problems in documentation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:105
#: d8488cb2e95a4e4e854a152968df1449
msgid "Diátaxis"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:112
#: 2d5621b7800c4fd281e69a3e6d81513d
msgid "The Diátaxis compass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:114
#: 3bcf4ec30d4b4dbf85e997c9f4eacb62
msgid "As you can see from the map:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:116
#: eaa3fc20792e40b786b438e548c56dbc
msgid "tutorials and how-to guides are concerned with what the user *does* (**action**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:117
#: e0f6cac6b530469cb534874382603410
msgid "reference and explanation are about what the user *knows* (**cognition**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:119
#: 40c7242a696a4d80878a732ba864d2dd
msgid "On the other hand:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:121
#: f5d4509319e049b7b47e006e7d49f2c5
msgid "tutorials and explanation serve the *acquistion* of skill (the user's **study**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:122
#: c4af3f7a2bcf4a61835f4295cdcad3ad
msgid "how-to guides and reference serve the *application* of skill (the user's **work**)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:124
#: c6c7a57b8aef41fea4ccac1e41d04e97
msgid "But a map doesn't tell you what to *do* - it's reference. To guide your action you need a different sort of tool, in this case, a kind of Diátaxis compass."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:128
#: 103997df81a144949852f74b22b2a84b
msgid ":ref:`The compass in more detail <compass>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:130
#: a41733c3019243caad062b3a9b7e6e9c
msgid "The compass is useful in two different ways."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:132
#: 5f509ff9c78a4628bc22f0b7834442f3
msgid "When creating documentation, it helps clarify your own intentions, and helps make sure you're actually doing what you think you're doing."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:134
#: 35efcaa7429a4fc4acfa530e78e67847
msgid "When looking at documentation, it helps understand what's going on in it, and makes problems stand out."
msgstr ""

#: ../../start-here.rst:136
#: 8662a8a650ec483cbd7a2716a7693048
msgid "The compass is not nearly as eye-catching as the map, but when you're at work puzzling over a documentation problem it's what will help you move forward."
msgstr ""

